Context: repair of the load-flake that failed T140's combined verification (make build && ./bin/ohya version && make check). Root cause 1 (product): Endpoint.closeDevice cancels the session context and then closes the connection; a handler woken by the cancellation could write one error frame inside that gap, so a revoked device received a protocol reply and TestRevocationCancelsInFlightRequest failed ("the in-flight request completed after revocation"). Fix: connSession.Write refuses writes once the session context is done, so every protocol reply goes through the session and a cancelled session sends nothing; the Serve-loop busy rejection stays raw because it answers a fresh, pre-session connection. The TLA+ Auth model covers registry/session state transitions, not frame writes, so no spec change. Root cause 2 (test): TestObserverCountsHubBatchStages asserted hub_ack_write_duration, which the server records after the ack bytes are on the wire; a preempted server goroutine lost the assertion. Fix: observertest.Recorder.AwaitDurationCount polls that one counter (all other asserted metrics are recorded before their client-visible reply). Evidence: combined-verification log in the repair feedback; reproduction reasoning in NOTES.md "Revocation teardown race".
